Relevant columns, their potential usage and important conditions  
• `npi_raw.provider_business_practice_location_address_city_name` : choose providers in “Mountain View”.  
• `npi_raw.provider_business_practice_location_address_state_name` : restrict to the state “CA”.  
• `npi_raw.healthcare_provider_taxonomy_code_1 … _15` : every NPI can list up to 15 taxonomy codes; we have to read all of them.  
• `healthcare_provider_taxonomy_code_set.code` : join‐key that links a taxonomy code to its textual description.  
• `healthcare_provider_taxonomy_code_set.specialization` : the specialization we need; keep rows where this field is not NULL / empty (‘’).  
• Condition examples  
  – `UPPER(provider_business_practice_location_address_city_name) = 'MOUNTAIN VIEW'`  
  – `provider_business_practice_location_address_state_name = 'CA'`  
  – `specialization IS NOT NULL AND specialization <> ''`  

Below are ten BigQuery SQL statements that start with very simple inspection queries and end with one self‑contained query that delivers the requested result.  All intermediate queries are limited to 20 rows (except the final answer).  

```sql
-- 1) Sample NPIs that list Mountain View, CA as the practice location
SELECT npi,
       provider_business_practice_location_address_city_name  AS city,
       provider_business_practice_location_address_state_name AS state
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.nppes.npi_raw`
WHERE  UPPER(provider_business_practice_location_address_city_name) = 'MOUNTAIN VIEW'
  AND  provider_business_practice_location_address_state_name = 'CA'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Look at the taxonomy code fields for those Mountain View providers
SELECT npi,
       healthcare_provider_taxonomy_code_1 AS tax1,
       healthcare_provider_taxonomy_code_2 AS tax2,
       healthcare_provider_taxonomy_code_3 AS tax3,
       healthcare_provider_taxonomy_code_4 AS tax4,
       healthcare_provider_taxonomy_code_5 AS tax5
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.nppes.npi_raw`
WHERE  UPPER(provider_business_practice_location_address_city_name) = 'MOUNTAIN VIEW'
  AND  provider_business_practice_location_address_state_name = 'CA'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
